 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. No, a century is 100 miles, and riding it is certainly an achievement. Many people take years planning it as a goal ride. If you ride average of fifteen miles per hour, it would take six hours including stops. It is, and it' good way to spend one. You' feel accomplishment and see lots of scenery. a good idea to start small and build up. Lots of people do, but the short ones don't build the same distance. Start with a park or trail system, and work up. Lots of rides, some shorter than the one you want to do, with breaks in between. Get your bike serviced regularly.",
